    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "annot-memvault-e3-3c91d7a4",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 5850,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 420,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-31 (memvault, slice E3 + its fresh-context review): api/src/memvault/ gains fts.ts - a\nPER-TENANT SQLite FTS5 index (better-sqlite3, the driver knowledge/index-store.ts already uses; no new\ndependency). Where knowledge/ keeps ONE table and filters every row/query by orgId, memvault keeps ONE\nDATABASE FILE PER USER at <userRoot>/.index/notes.db: no shared table exists for a missing predicate to\nexpose. fts.ts -> store.ts -> jail.ts, one direction, no cycle; fts.ts imports NO node:path (grep gate).\nTwo new ops on the router: POST /search (JSON) and GET /export (kind:'binary'), a tar of MARKDOWN ONLY\nwritten by archiver ('tar' backend of the existing api dependency) - .index/ is a dot-dir the walk never\nsees, so it is excluded by construction, not by filter.\nCONTAINMENT IS FILE-GRANULAR, NOT DIRECTORY-GRANULAR. jail.indexDbFile checks the DATABASE FILE and each\nSQLite sidecar (-wal/-shm/-journal), the same treatment notePath gives a note; checking only the .index\nDIRECTORY left a planted notes.db symlink pointing one tenant's index at another's (read leak AND write\npoisoning). jail.realTargetOf additionally fails closed on a DANGLING link: realpath cannot resolve one,\nand falling back to the parent reported it as contained while open(O_CREAT) would follow it and create\nthe file at the target - a write primitive outside the tenant.\nHANDLE CACHE IS REFERENCE-COUNTED. The bound (32) is a soft target: only IDLE entries are ever evicted,\nand a condemned entry leaves the map at once but is closed by its last borrower. Closing a handle an\nin-flight operation still held turned ordinary concurrent load past the bound into HTTP 500s.\nINDEX STALENESS HAS A REAL RECOVERY. A failed maintain discards the index (fts.invalidate) AND every cache\nmiss reconciles the row count against the markdown (fts.isStale) - previously a valid-but-stale index\nopened cleanly and under-reported the owner's vault forever, across restarts.\nE2-REVIEW CORRECTIONS also carried here: jail anchors containment on realpath(<memvaultRoot>)+'/'+userId;\nthe walk enters through jail.resolvedUserRoot; service.guard() funnels every non-jail failure to an\naudited 'error' + INTERNAL envelope; routes audit schema refusals as 'denied'; server.ts has a terminal\nErrorEnvelope middleware after the /api/v1 routers.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-31 (memvault, slice E3 + its fresh-context review): api/src/memvault/ gains fts.ts - a\nPER-TENANT SQLite FTS5 index (better-sqlite3, the driver knowledge/index-store.ts already uses; no new\ndependency). Where knowledge/ keeps ONE table and filters every row/query by orgId, memvault keeps ONE\nDATABASE FILE PER USER at <userRoot>/.index/notes.db: no shared table exists for a missing predicate to\nexpose. fts.ts -> store.ts -> jail.ts, one direction, no cycle; fts.ts imports NO node:path (grep gate).\nTwo new ops on the router: POST /search (JSON) and GET /export (kind:'binary'), a tar of MARKDOWN ONLY\nwritten by archiver ('tar' backend of the existing api dependency) - .index/ is a dot-dir the walk never\nsees, so it is excluded by construction, not by filter.\nCONTAINMENT IS FILE-GRANULAR, NOT DIRECTORY-GRANULAR. jail.indexDbFile checks the DATABASE FILE and each\nSQLite sidecar (-wal/-shm/-journal), the same treatment notePath gives a note; checking only the .index\nDIRECTORY left a planted notes.db symlink pointing one tenant's index at another's (read leak AND write\npoisoning). jail.realTargetOf additionally fails closed on a DANGLING link: realpath cannot resolve one,\nand falling back to the parent reported it as contained while open(O_CREAT) would follow it and create\nthe file at the target - a write primitive outside the tenant.\nHANDLE CACHE IS REFERENCE-COUNTED. The bound (32) is a soft target: only IDLE entries are ever evicted,\nand a condemned entry leaves the map at once but is closed by its last borrower. Closing a handle an\nin-flight operation still held turned ordinary concurrent load past the bound into HTTP 500s.\nINDEX STALENESS HAS A REAL RECOVERY. A failed maintain discards the index (fts.invalidate) AND every cache\nmiss reconciles the row count against the markdown (fts.isStale) - previously a valid-but-stale index\nopened cleanly and under-reported the owner's vault forever, across restarts.\nE2-REVIEW CORRECTIONS also carried here: jail anchors containment on realpath(<memvaultRoot>)+'/'+userId;\nthe walk enters through jail.resolvedUserRoot; service.guard() funnels every non-jail failure to an\naudited 'error' + INTERNAL envelope; routes audit schema refusals as 'denied'; server.ts has a terminal\nErrorEnvelope middleware after the /api/v1 routers.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-31 (memvault, slice E3 + its fresh-context review): api/src/memvault/ gains fts.ts - a\nPER-TENANT SQLite FTS5 index (better-sqlite3, the driver knowledge/index-store.ts already uses; no new\ndependency). Where knowledge/ keeps ONE table and filters every row/query by orgId, memvault keeps ONE\nDATABASE FILE PER USER at <userRoot>/.index/notes.db: no shared table exists for a missing predicate to\nexpose. fts.ts -> store.ts -> jail.ts, one direction, no cycle; fts.ts imports NO node:path (grep gate).\nTwo new ops on the router: POST /search (JSON) and GET /export (kind:'binary'), a tar of MARKDOWN ONLY\nwritten by archiver ('tar' backend of the existing api dependency) - .index/ is a dot-dir the walk never\nsees, so it is excluded by construction, not by filter.\nCONTAINMENT IS FILE-GRANULAR, NOT DIRECTORY-GRANULAR. jail.indexDbFile checks the DATABASE FILE and each\nSQLite sidecar (-wal/-shm/-journal), the same treatment notePath gives a note; checking only the .index\nDIRECTORY left a planted notes.db symlink pointing one tenant's index at another's (read leak AND write\npoisoning). jail.realTargetOf additionally fails closed on a DANGLING link: realpath cannot resolve one,\nand falling back to the parent reported it as contained while open(O_CREAT) would follow it and create\nthe file at the target - a write primitive outside the tenant.\nHANDLE CACHE IS REFERENCE-COUNTED. The bound (32) is a soft target: only IDLE entries are ever evicted,\nand a condemned entry leaves the map at once but is closed by its last borrower. Closing a handle an\nin-flight operation still held turned ordinary concurrent load past the bound into HTTP 500s.\nINDEX STALENESS HAS A REAL RECOVERY. A failed maintain discards the index (fts.invalidate) AND every cache\nmiss reconciles the row count against the markdown (fts.isStale) - previously a valid-but-stale index\nopened cleanly and under-reported the owner's vault forever, across restarts.\nE2-REVIEW CORRECTIONS also carried here: jail anchors containment on realpath(<memvaultRoot>)+'/'+userId;\nthe walk enters through jail.resolvedUserRoot; service.guard() funnels every non-jail failure to an\naudited 'error' + INTERNAL envelope; routes audit schema refusals as 'denied'; server.ts has a terminal\nErrorEnvelope middleware after the /api/v1 routers.",
      "fontSize": 14,
